WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.738
Exam day: pacing, elimination and the last week.

2
00:00:03.738 --> 00:00:12.980
Most people who fall short run out of time or second-guess good answers, so a pacing plan and an elimination habit are worth real points.

3
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:20.098
On the day, you sit the exam through Pearson VUE, either online with OnVUE or at a test centre.

4
00:00:20.098 --> 00:00:25.455
You get one hundred and twenty minutes to answer, with some extra seat time for check in.

5
00:00:25.455 --> 00:00:30.210
It is closed book with no AI tools, though online you get a digital whiteboard.

6
00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.919
Your score appears on screen when you finish.

7
00:00:34.319 --> 00:00:35.621
Here is a pacing plan.

8
00:00:35.621 --> 00:00:40.595
You have two minutes per question at most, so aim to commit in about ninety seconds.

9
00:00:40.595 --> 00:00:44.563
Read the actual question first, then the scenario details you need.

10
00:00:44.563 --> 00:00:48.175
If you are stuck, pick your best answer, flag it and move on.

11
00:00:48.175 --> 00:00:51.491
Keep about fifteen minutes at the end for flagged items.

12
00:00:51.491 --> 00:00:53.327
And never leave anything blank.

13
00:00:54.727 --> 00:00:57.791
When several answers look plausible, eliminate.

14
00:00:57.791 --> 00:01:01.702
Remove options about topics the guide says are out of scope.

15
00:01:01.702 --> 00:01:05.484
Remove prompt only fixes when a rule must hold every time.

16
00:01:05.484 --> 00:01:09.395
Remove options that swallow errors or guess at missing data.

17
00:01:09.395 --> 00:01:14.545
Then, among what remains, choose the simplest option that fixes the root cause.

18
00:01:15.945 --> 00:01:20.022
In the final week, sit two full timed mock exams a few days apart.

19
00:01:20.022 --> 00:01:24.531
Use the domain breakdown to pick your two weakest domains and drill them.

20
00:01:24.531 --> 00:01:26.075
Clear the Mistake Clinic.

21
00:01:26.075 --> 00:01:30.707
Revisit the lesson for any task statement still under seventy five percent.

22
00:01:30.707 --> 00:01:36.575
And if you are testing online, run the system check and prepare your room and ID ahead of time.

23
00:01:37.975 --> 00:01:39.026
Three last traps.

24
00:01:39.026 --> 00:01:43.728
Do not sink five minutes into one question, because they all count the same.

25
00:01:43.728 --> 00:01:48.245
During review, only change an answer when you can name a concrete reason.

26
00:01:48.245 --> 00:01:57.772
And remember that the exam follows the guide's terminology, even where the documentation has since renamed something, like the Task tool now called Agent.

27
00:01:59.172 --> 00:01:59.870
To wrap up.

28
00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:02.981
Commit in about ninety seconds, flag and move on.

29
00:02:02.981 --> 00:02:04.251
Never leave a blank.

30
00:02:04.251 --> 00:02:10.218
Eliminate out of scope and prompt only options first, then choose the simplest root cause fix.

31
00:02:10.218 --> 00:02:12.313
Answer in the exam guide's terms.

32
00:02:12.313 --> 00:02:16.884
When you are ready, sit the mock exam in the game under real conditions.

33
00:02:16.884 --> 00:02:17.519
Good luck.

